     5	A stranger arrives knowing that the Fed unanimously raised rates by a quarter point, probably remembering that the new range tops out at 4 percent and that this was the first increase since 2023. The coverage makes it easy to read the move as a simple attempt to undo an oil-driven price shock and the 4.1 percent projection as a settled path for rates. They do not yet know what changed since July, what rate policy can and cannot change, or how much one increase reaches their own finances.
